+# Loyalty Backend Handoff
+
+| Priority | Missing capability / verification  | Requirement                         | Current frontend behavior and API evidence                                                                                         | Exact request                                                                                                                                                          | Blocks                                  |
+| -------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
+| P0       | Guest claim days                   | Settings field specification        | Field is absent from settings GET, PUT, and history. The UI does not fabricate it.                                                 | Add a documented `0..365` field to current settings, save, and version values. Define `0` semantics.                                                                   | Guest-claim setting                     |
+| P0       | Never-expiring points              | Settings field specification        | `validity_months` is documented only as an integer; null/no-expiry behavior is unknown. The UI exposes finite validity only.       | Define GET/PUT/history representation and warning-days behavior for never-expiring points.                                                                             | No-expiry option                        |
+| P0       | Atomic debit/security invariants   | Customer AC-01 and financial safety | UI rejects a debit above the last known available balance, but concurrent safety cannot be client-enforced.                        | Verify endpoint authorization, transactional nonnegative debit, immutable ledger/audit creation, and idempotency/replay behavior. Document validation response fields. | Safe production adjustment verification |
+| P0       | Adjustment order link              | Customer story field                | POST has no order field and ledger `order` is null in all examples. The UI sends no invented field.                                | Add/document an optional order identifier, ownership validation, and the non-null ledger order response shape.                                                         | Related-order control and link          |
+| P1       | Remaining reason codes             | Adjustment reason list              | Only `customer_service` and `other` are documented and displayed.                                                                  | Publish official codes and labels for order-problem compensation and balance-error correction.                                                                         | Two reason choices                      |
+| P1       | Ledger types and pagination        | Ledger filters/pagination           | Only documented filters (`type`, `from`, `to`) are sent. Pagination meta exists, but request args and full enum are undocumented.  | Publish all event/filter enums, sort order, date inclusivity/time zone, and supported `page`/`per_page` parameters.                                                    | Full filters and pagination controls    |
+| P1       | CSV export                         | Customer ledger flow                | No export endpoint exists; frontend intentionally does not export only the visible page.                                           | Provide a current-filter export endpoint or approve/document a bounded all-pages strategy.                                                                             | CSV export                              |
+| P1       | Expiring-soon semantics            | Summary                             | Null is shown as unavailable; a returned object is shown without adding it to balances.                                            | Define empty/null forms and what `expires_at` means when multiple lots qualify.                                                                                        | Exact expiry explanation                |
+| P1       | Deleted/blocked customers          | Customer AS-01/AS-02                | Frozen status is displayed and adjustment submission is allowed to reach backend. Deleted-customer shape is unknown.               | Document anonymized deleted-customer response and adjustment prohibition; verify blocked adjustments and frozen redemption semantics.                                  | Deleted-customer read-only UX           |
+| P1       | Notification delivery              | Customer AC-04                      | Frontend sends `notify_customer`; success copy confirms the adjustment, not delivery.                                              | Define synchronous/queued delivery semantics and failure reporting.                                                                                                    | Delivery confirmation                   |
+| P1       | Settings concurrency and lifecycle | Settings AC-02/03/05, AS-03         | Latest `version_id`, explicit disable confirmation, and conflict-preserving UI are implemented. Samples do not prove server rules. | Verify stale-version rejection, first-launch permanence, disable effects, re-enable behavior, and historical non-recalculation.                                        | Backend acceptance evidence             |
+| P1       | Earning/expiry math                | Settings AC-01/04                   | Preview uses documented nominal math; client validation uses documented ranges.                                                    | Define earned-point rounding/precision, calendar-month warning comparison, and credit-lot expiry calculation.                                                          | Exact parity for edge cases             |
+| P1       | History pagination/sorting         | Settings history                    | UI fetches history only when active using the documented `per_page=20`.                                                            | Document `page`, sorting guarantee, and stable pagination behavior.                                                                                                    | Multi-page history                      |
+| P2       | High-return warning decision       | Proposed Settings AS-01             | Not implemented because the story marks it proposed and no request flag exists.                                                    | Confirm or reject the product requirement and threshold behavior.                                                                                                      | Optional warning UX                     |
+
+The existing Laravel validation envelope is sufficient and is already reused; a new generic error contract is not requested.
+
+Authorization is backend-owned. The frontend intentionally adds no RBAC, capability hooks, or control-visibility rules and relies on the existing standard 401/403 handling.
